You are working in the git repository checked out at /luxon (the Luxon date/time library, JavaScript, jest tests). Do NOT use the internet. Do NOT consult any other copy of luxon (e.g. under node_modules) for reference.

GOAL: Fix a bug in /luxon/src/impl/util.js so that a hidden test named "DateTime#toISODate() correctly pads negative years" passes. Only /luxon/src/impl/util.js may be modified. Do NOT modify or delete any test file, and do not reformat unrelated code. NOTE: another agent has already changed a DIFFERENT function (objToLocalTS) in this same file; leave that change alone and do not revert it.

DIAGNOSIS (verify it yourself): `padStart` in /luxon/src/impl/util.js is:

    export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
      if (input.toString().length < n) {
        return ("0".repeat(n) + input).slice(-n);
      } else {
        return input.toString();
      }
    }

For negative numbers this produces garbage: padStart(-5, 4) returns "00-5" instead of "-0005". Because the "yyyy" formatter token uses padStart(dt.year, 4), `DateTime.fromObject({ year: -5, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate()` currently returns "00-5-05-25" instead of the correct ISO 8601 expanded form "-0005-05-25".

REQUIRED FIX: make padStart handle negative input by padding the absolute value and prefixing the sign, i.e.:

    export function padStart(input, n = 2) {
      const isNeg = input < 0;
      let padded;
      if (isNeg) {
        padded = "-" + ("" + -input).padStart(n, "0");
      } else {
        padded = ("" + input).padStart(n, "0");
      }
      return padded;
    }

Do not change anything else in the file.

STEPS:
1. Run the baseline suite first and record failures: `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -40`. Known pre-existing failures: 2 tests in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js (French locale hour padding). Those must remain the ONLY failures.
2. Apply the edit to /luxon/src/impl/util.js only.
3. Re-run `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -40` and confirm no new failures; also run `npx jest test/datetime test/duration test/interval test/info test/zones`.
4. Verify with a scratch script (create /tmp/checkpad.js, run with `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/checkpad.js`; delete it afterwards and make sure `git status --porcelain` shows only modified src files and no untracked files):
   - DateTime.fromObject({ year: -5, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate() === "-0005-05-25"
   - DateTime.fromObject({ year: -5, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISO() starts with "-0005-05-25T"
   - DateTime.fromObject({ year: -118040, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate() === "-118040-05-25" (existing test)
   - DateTime.fromObject({ year: 118040, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toISODate() === "+118040-05-25" (existing test)
   - DateTime.utc(1982, 5, 25).toISODate() === "1982-05-25"; DateTime.fromObject({ year: 3, month: 1, day: 1, zone: "utc" }).toISODate() === "0003-01-01"
   - Also check toFormat: DateTime.fromObject({ year: -21, month: 5, day: 25, zone: "utc" }).toFormat("yyyy") === "-0021", and that DateTime.utc(1982,5,25).toFormat("yyyy") === "1982" and .set({ year: 3 }).toFormat("yyyy") === "0003".
5. Run `npx eslint src/impl/util.js`.

REPORT BACK: the exact `git diff` for the padStart hunk (do not revert or report the other agent's objToLocalTS hunk as yours), baseline vs post-fix jest summary, the scratch-check outputs, and confirmation that `git status --porcelain` shows only modified src files and no untracked files.

You are working in the git repository checked out at /luxon (the Luxon date/time library, JavaScript, jest tests). Do NOT use the internet. Do NOT consult any other copy of luxon (e.g. under node_modules) for reference.

GOAL: Fix a bug in /luxon/src/datetime.js so that a hidden test named "DateTime#isInDST() returns true for 1974 whole year in USA- from January 6th to October 27th" passes. Only /luxon/src/datetime.js may be modified. Do NOT modify or delete any test file, and do not reformat unrelated code.

DIAGNOSIS (verify it yourself): the `isInDST` getter (around line 1164) is:

    get isInDST() {
      if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
        return false;
      } else {
        return (
          this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
        );
      }
    }

`set({ month: 1 })` keeps the day of month. For a DateTime that is itself in January (or in May), the comparison is made against the very same instant, so it can never be greater, and isInDST wrongly returns false. This breaks the USA in 1974, when DST ran year-round from Jan 6 to Oct 27: e.g. DateTime.fromISO("1974-01-15", { zone: "America/New_York" }).isInDST is currently false but must be true, and likewise for any date in May 1974.

REQUIRED FIX: change `this.set({ month: 1 })` to `this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 })` in the isInDST getter (leave the `month: 5` comparison as it is). This makes the January comparison use Jan 1, which is a standard-time reference in the northern hemisphere.

STEPS:
1. Run the baseline suite first and record failures: `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -40`. Known pre-existing failures: 2 tests in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js (French locale hour padding). Those must remain the ONLY failures.
2. Apply the edit to /luxon/src/datetime.js only.
3. Re-run `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -40` and confirm no new failures; also run `npx jest test/datetime/zone.test.js test/info`.
4. Verify behaviour with a scratch script (create /tmp/checkdst.js, run with `cd /luxon && npx babel-node /tmp/checkdst.js`; delete it afterwards and ensure `git status --porcelain` shows only ` M src/datetime.js`):
   - For every day from 1974-01-01 to 1974-12-31, compute DateTime.fromISO(date, { zone: "America/New_York" }).isInDST and assert it is true exactly for 1974-01-06 .. 1974-10-27 and false otherwise. Print any mismatches.
   - Check the existing expectations still hold: DateTime.fromISO("1982-05-25T09:23:54", { zone: "America/Los_Angeles" }).set({ month: 1 }).isInDST === false, .set({ month: 5 }).isInDST === true, .set({ month: 12 }).isInDST === false.
   - Check a southern-hemisphere zone: for 2017 in Australia/Sydney, isInDST should be true in January and false in July.
5. Run `npx eslint src/datetime.js`.

REPORT BACK: the exact `git diff` you applied, baseline vs post-fix jest summary, the scratch-check outputs (including the list of any mismatching 1974 dates), and confirmation that `git status --porcelain` shows only ` M src/datetime.js`.
